id: smp
package: bluetooth_le_siwx91x
description: >
  SMP (Security Manager Protocol) event handlers for BLE
label: SMP
category: Device|Si91x|Wireless|BLE|SMP
quality: production
metadata:
  sbom:
    license: Zlib
component_root_path: ./components/device/silabs/si91x/wireless/smp
provides:
  - name: smp
define:
  - name: SL_SI91X_BLE_SMP_COMPONENT
source:
  - path: src/smp_user_event_hdlrs.c
  - path: src/smp_init.c
  - path: src/smp_utilities.c

include:
  - path: inc
    file_list:
      - path: smp.h

config_file:
  - path: inc/smp_config.h
    directory: ble_config
    file_id: smp_config

requires:
  - name: ble_unified_framework
  - name: gap

template_contribution:
  - name: ble_unified_config_includes
    value: "smp_config.h"
  - name: ble_unified_init_hooks
    value:
      ble_unified_init_func: ble_smp_init
      ble_unified_init_label: "SMP"
  - name: wrapper_implementations
    value:
      name: sl_btc_ble_smp_register_callbacks_wrapper
      registration_api: rsi_ble_smp_register_callbacks
      callbacks:
        - event_smp_req
        - event_smp_resp
        - event_smp_passkey
        - event_smp_failed
        - event_encryption_enabled
        - event_smp_passkey_display
        - event_sc_passkey
        - event_le_ltk_request
        - event_le_security_keys
        - NULL
        - NULL
  - name: ble_events
    value:
      event_smp_req:
        callback_params:
          - name: rsi_bt_event_smp_req
            type: rsi_bt_event_smp_req_p
        event_data:
          name: rsi_bt_event_smp_req
      
      event_smp_resp:
        callback_params:
          - name: rsi_bt_event_smp_resp
            type: rsi_bt_event_smp_resp_p
        event_data:
          name: rsi_bt_event_smp_resp
      
      event_smp_passkey:
        callback_params:
          - name: rsi_bt_event_smp_passkey
            type: rsi_bt_event_smp_passkey_p
        event_data:
          name: rsi_bt_event_smp_passkey
      
      event_smp_failed:
        callback_params:
          - name: status
            type: uint16_t
          - name: rsi_bt_event_smp_failed
            type: rsi_bt_event_smp_failed_p
        event_data:
          name: rsi_bt_event_smp_failed
      
      event_encryption_enabled:
        callback_params:
          - name: status
            type: uint16_t
          - name: rsi_bt_event_encryption_enabled
            type: rsi_bt_event_encryption_enabled_p
        event_data:
          name: rsi_bt_event_encryption_enabled
      
      event_smp_passkey_display:
        callback_params:
          - name: rsi_bt_event_smp_passkey_display
            type: rsi_bt_event_smp_passkey_display_p
        event_data:
          name: rsi_bt_event_smp_passkey_display
      
      event_sc_passkey:
        callback_params:
          - name: rsi_bt_event_sc_passkey
            type: rsi_bt_event_sc_passkey_p
        event_data:
          name: rsi_bt_event_sc_passkey
      
      event_le_ltk_request:
        callback_params:
          - name: rsi_bt_event_le_ltk_request
            type: rsi_bt_event_le_ltk_request_p
        event_data:
          name: rsi_bt_event_le_ltk_request
      
      event_le_security_keys:
        callback_params:
          - name: rsi_bt_event_le_security_keys
            type: rsi_bt_event_le_security_keys_p
        event_data:
          name: rsi_bt_event_le_security_keys
      
      event_smp_pending:
        callback_params:
          - name: conn_id
            type: uint8_t*
        event_data:
          name: conn_id
  - name: agents_slab
    value:
      id: smp
      context: |
        ## SMP Component (Si91x Wireless BLE Unified)
        Security Manager Protocol — pairing, bonding, and link encryption. Pulls in `gap` (connection table) and `ble_unified_framework` (event loop). Defines `SL_SI91X_BLE_SMP_COMPONENT` so optional SMP code paths in other components compile only when SMP is selected.
        ### Init hook
        - Function: `ble_smp_init` (registered via `ble_unified_init_hooks`).
        - Registers SMP callback wrapper `sl_btc_ble_smp_register_callbacks_wrapper()` covering: `event_smp_req`, `event_smp_resp`, `event_smp_passkey`, `event_smp_failed`, `event_encryption_enabled`, `event_smp_passkey_display`, `event_sc_passkey`, `event_le_ltk_request`, `event_le_security_keys`.
        ### Configuration (`smp_config.h` — copied to `config/ble_config/`)
        Key macros: `MITM_ENABLE` (Man-in-the-Middle protection), `RSI_BLE_SMP_IO_CAPABILITY` (e.g. `KEYBOARD_ONLY`, `DISPLAY_ONLY`, `KEYBOARD_DISPLAY`, `NO_INPUT_NO_OUTPUT`), `RSI_BLE_APP_SMP_PASSKEY`, secure-connection toggles. The IO capability dictates which pairing method is selected by the BLE controller (Just Works, Passkey Entry, Numeric Comparison, OOB).
        ### Pairing Workflow (Central-initiated)
        1. After `event_conn_status`/`event_enhance_conn_status` indicates a connection.
        2. Set capabilities: `rsi_ble_set_smp_pairing_cap_data()`.
        3. Initiate: `rsi_ble_smp_pair_request()`.
        4. On `event_smp_req` / `event_smp_resp`: respond via `rsi_ble_smp_pair_response()`.
        5. On `event_smp_passkey` / `event_smp_passkey_display`: send passkey with `rsi_ble_smp_passkey()`.
        6. On `event_encryption_enabled`: link is encrypted; LTK is exchanged in `event_le_security_keys`.
        ### Common Mistakes to Avoid
        - Initiating pairing before the GAP connection is fully established (wait for `event_enhance_conn_status` with status==success).
        - Setting `MITM_ENABLE=1` with `NO_INPUT_NO_OUTPUT` IO capability — controller will fall back to Just Works (no MITM) and the configuration is effectively ignored.
        - Forgetting to handle `event_smp_failed` — pairing can fail for many reasons (MITM mismatch, OOB unavailable, DH-key check failed); the connection stays up but is unencrypted.
        - Calling SMP APIs without `gatt_client` selected when the remote requires service discovery as part of bonding flows.
    priority: -5304
